# Moving the Factory product into the Lab

## 1. What travels

The Factory's engine product is the **car**. A profiler, builder or benchmark CC is a reusable tool used to produce or assess that car. CC calls can carry the product handoff as typed artifacts. The product can contain zero reusable CCs.

The Lab receives a product manifest plus access to immutable bytes. The manifest identifies the candidate, delivery representation, build/source lineage, compatibility requirements and available evidence. It refers to the actual binary or source payload; a human narrative is insufficient.

| Delivery representation | Sufficient identity | Lab action |
|---|---|---|
| Native engine component | Component manifest and payload digest, entrypoint, ABI/platform, required runtime and libraries. | Verify and stage the native package; select it explicitly at restart. |
| OCI engine image | Platform-specific image digest, startup/configuration contract and external input references. | Pull/import verified bytes and start the pinned image. |
| Source snapshot | Immutable tree/archive, submodule/LFS/blob materials, build recipe, toolchain and dependency lock. | Execute an authorized build stage, freeze its product, then measure it. |
| Git change set | Exact base plus complete patch/blob set and expected resulting tree digest. | Apply in an isolated worktree; verify the resulting tree; build and freeze. |

A Git diff is sufficient only as a reconstruction recipe with a known base and all required material. Ordinary text diffs can omit untracked files, binaries, file modes, submodules and LFS objects. Unanchored diffs must not identify a measurement candidate.

## 2. Preserve Strata's native package

Strata's `engine-component.json` schema 2 describes immutable native engine directories, file hashes/sizes, entrypoint, platform/backend, architecture targets and runtime/driver requirements. Use that existing manifest as the engine format; reference it from the product rather than duplicating its fields. Its component hash manifest excludes the manifest itself; the outer artifact reference can identify the whole delivered archive separately.

Reviewed local Strata revision: `c62d5e3a15b40ea51c96aae9e8d36928965f53ab`, `packaging/ENGINE-COMPONENT.md`, `packaging/package_engine.py` and `strata_control/engine_component.py`. Native local packages can be unsigned; release-feed signatures are a different policy. Lab admission must apply its own trust policy. A loader's compatible fallback must not silently replace the candidate selected for comparison.

The existing Spark build path targets Linux ARM64/SM121 and a particular CUDA/driver baseline. Those requirements belong to the pinned engine/build and qualified environment. They are not mandatory fields for every CC. Normalize platform vocabulary explicitly: native `linux-aarch64` and OCI `linux/arm64` describe corresponding targets through a defined mapping.

## 3. End-to-end handoff

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant R as Requester
    participant F as Factory coding agent
    participant S as Artifact store
    participant L as Lab agent
    participant H as Qualified Spark host
    participant E as Evaluator
    R->>F: Product brief and optional CC requests
    F->>F: Implement, pin source, build and self-test
    F->>S: Product, materials and build provenance
    F-->>L: Product reference and Factory receipt
    L->>S: Fetch and verify required bytes
    L->>H: Admit, stage, restart exact candidate
    H-->>L: Loaded binary/configuration and generation
    L->>H: Invoke pinned measurement CC
    H->>S: Raw evidence and attempt receipt
    L->>E: Evidence, candidate identity and frozen policy
    E-->>R: Pass, fail or inconclusive comparison
```

The payloads use ordinary CC typed input/output ports. A Factory operation takes a brief/request artifact and returns a product reference plus an optional list of CC release references. A Lab preparation operation takes the product and environment requirements and returns an instance handle. A measurement operation takes that handle, model and workload. Each operation has its own prerequisites and effects; the Factory's grants do not carry into the Lab.

## 4. Minimum product-to-measurement joins

These are required meanings for the handoff profile, not duplicate top-level fields on every capsule. Native manifests and existing provenance records remain authoritative.

| Owner | Fact recorded once | Referenced by |
|---|---|---|
| Factory | Source revision/tree and all local changes, recipe, build inputs and produced artifact. | Product manifest and build record. |
| Product | Delivery representation, payload Ref and native manifest/schema Ref. | Lab preparation call. |
| Lab admission | Policy version, eligible host/provider, requested candidate and resource reservation. | Bound preparation/measurement calls. |
| Lab host | Actual loaded binary/component, effective configuration, instance generation and restart event. | Measurement subject and receipt. |
| Measurement CC | Actual measurement window, workload evidence, output coverage and sensor gaps. | Receipt and evaluation. |
| Evaluator | Frozen criteria, baseline, evidence references and verdict. | Promotion decision. |

Before measuring a locally adjusted Muse instance, link parent image/component → patch or configuration delta → resulting tree/configuration → rebuilt binary or snapshot → restart → process generation → measured window. Model shards, tokenizer, quantization, workload, cache policy and environment are independently pinned inputs. A parent image or PID alone is insufficient.

## 5. Edge cases with defined outcomes

| Case | Outcome and owner |
|---|---|
| Source provided but no compiler/toolchain available | Lab preparation blocks `MISSING_BUILD_ENVIRONMENT`; it does not treat source delivery as runnable. |
| Patch base differs or untracked dependency is absent | Factory/Lab reconstruction rejects `SOURCE_MISMATCH` or `MISSING_MATERIAL`. No fuzzy apply for scored candidates. |
| ARM64 engine sent to wrong host; CUDA or ABI mismatch | Admission blocks `INCOMPATIBLE_ABI` before launch. |
| Loader falls back to a previous engine | Loaded identity check rejects `CANDIDATE_MISMATCH`; do not label the result with the requested candidate. |
| Local configuration changed but endpoint not restarted | Preparation reports `STALE_INSTANCE`; either restart with authority or keep the attempt ineligible. |
| PID reused, engine hot-reloaded or endpoint rerouted mid-capture | Verify generation/deployment throughout capture. Split evidence by generation or mark identity coverage inconclusive. |
| Tensor-parallel engine has several workers | Bind the worker set and rank-to-binary/configuration map. Replacement workers create a changed subject. |
| JIT kernels or runtime-selected backend change executable behavior | Record JIT/toolchain/cache key and resolved backend; retain generated binary digest where available. Incomplete identity limits reproducibility claims. |
| External weights unavailable or access revoked | Block model binding; never silently substitute a smaller model. |
| GPU shared with another workload | Record isolation/contamination evidence. Enforce comparison policy; a completed run can be unsuitable for performance claims. |
| Warm cache differs between arms | Apply frozen warm/cold policy and record cache preparation. Do not explain away a regression after seeing results. |
| Profiler cannot attach in a container | Select an authorized host provider or block `PREREQUISITE_UNAVAILABLE`. No implicit privileged fallback. |
| Profiler perturbs timing | Declare the effect; separate instrumented diagnostics from uninstrumented scoring where the policy requires it. |
| Crash after restart but before acknowledgment | Reconcile actual process and effect journal. Do not retry restart blindly. |
| A2A disconnects while a build continues | Reattach to the durable task/call; do not create a second build by default. |
| Cancellation races with product publication | Keep the immutable product and actual completion history; reconcile publication/stop order. Cancellation cannot erase effects. |
| Metrics are valid but candidate misses its target | Execution succeeds; independent evaluation fails. Preserve useful negative evidence for RSI. |
| Consumer cannot retrieve evidence | Return explicit unavailable evidence/assessment, preserving references. A producer's summary is not equivalent evidence. |

## 6. Why this helps RSI

Each iteration has a reconstructible change, actual executed subject and comparable evidence. The next coding agent can distinguish a bad change from a failed build, wrong binary, contaminated benchmark or inadequate trace. A successful modification can become a reusable CC; an improved engine can remain a software product. Neither automatically changes the evaluator or promotion policy.

Keep the mandatory floor small: identity, typed ports, explicit effects, bounded execution, durable result and lineage. Add stronger checks through consumer policy and relevant profiles. The default must reveal absent evidence rather than fabricate assurance.

## 7. Delivery status

This is a proposed handoff profile grounded in source inspection. The core declaration fixtures still use image-backed CC tools. Native engine packaging is a product format, not a newly implemented CC execution provider. A real Factory→Spark→Muse restart and measurement trial remains required.
